      "reason": "Resolve feature alignment and distinguish training memorization from useful ranking discrimination before implementing the adapter.",
      "query": "In SASRec next-item recommendation diagnostics using training-derived prefix/target pairs, how should left padding, sequence truncation, repeated targets, final-position feature extraction, and candidate scoring shapes be handled? What sanity checks detect target leakage and distinguish training-fit ranks from generalization without changing the existing validation split?"
